# Environment
.env
.env.*
# `.env` and `.env.*` only cover names that START with `.env` — `.env.*` matches `.env.production`
# but NOT `AutoJMS-API.env`. A real secrets file (JWT_PRIVATE_KEY, API_SIGNATURE_SECRET) was
# sitting untracked and unignored at backend/render-license-server/AutoJMS-API.env, one `git add .`
# away from this PUBLIC repo, and eng/harness/check-secrets.ps1 could not catch it: step 2 scans
# TRACKED files and step 3 scans STAGED files, so an untracked file is scanned by neither and the
# gate reported PASS with the key on disk. These two patterns close the name shape, not the gate.
#
# Both match at ANY depth: a gitignore pattern with no slash in it applies to every directory
# level below, so one rule here covers backend/, src/ and any future folder.
#
# `*.env.*` also matches `.env.example` — that is fine only because the `!.env.example` /
# `!.env.staging.example` / `!.env.production.example` negations live BELOW this block and the
# last matching pattern wins. Never move those negations above this line.
*.env
*.env.*
appsettings.*.json

# Firebase/DataHub keys - NEVER COMMIT
serviceAccountKey.json
service_account.json
serviceAccountKey.*.json
firebase-adminsdk*.json
*.firebase-adminsdk.json
!serviceAccountKey.example.json
*-key.json
*service*.json
!.env.example
!.env.staging.example
!.env.production.example
*.sec

